  <h1>A 7M-Param Model That Beats<br>GPT-5 at Reasoning Puzzles</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Probabilistic TRM (PTRM) takes a tiny 7M-parameter model and gives it one superpower: inject Gaussian noise into its hidden state, run K parallel guesses, and let the model pick its own best answer. Result: 91.2% on pencil puzzles — beating a 7-LLM ensemble at <em>0.0001× the cost</em>.
  </p>
  <div class="post-hero-meta">
