<h3>Limitations</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Only tested on reasoning <em>puzzles</em> with unique, verifiable answers — not open-ended generation.</li>
  <li>ARC-AGI-2 gains are modest (+1.1pp) because the Q head is weaker at identifying correct solutions for these harder visual tasks.</li>
  <li>Grid size limited to 9×9 (Sudoku) and 10×10 (others) due to compute constraints.</li>
  <li>The method works best when the Q head can reliably distinguish correct from incorrect answers — a stronger verifier is an open research direction.</li>
</ul>
</section>

